  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Beat the press – 4v4 with a pressing joker",
  "description": "Play 4v4 with goalkeepers on a full rink. On top of that there is a defensive joker (J) who always presses the team with the puck – so the team in possession has five opponents to beat. The leader starts play from one team's defensive corner, and that team has to play its way out of the pressure in the tight space and switch play quickly.\n\nIf the joker wins the puck, they hit it out over the boards. At every stoppage the leader restarts from the other team's defensive corner.\n\nIdeally play with three teams, where the third team provides the joker and sends in a new joker at each restart. Make sure every team gets the joker role equally often. The drill can also be used to practise aggressive pressing in the offensive zone. In the picture the joker is red with a J, but they press both teams. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Play your way out of the pressure – no long hopeful pucks."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Talk to each other: who is free, where is the space?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Move to offer short passing options close to the player on the puck."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Switch play quickly when the pressure is drawn to one side."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
